PatchClosure-Bench repro — apache-shiro-cve-2020-13933
CVE-2020-11989 (V1=incomplete fix, TARGET) -> CVE-2020-13933 (V2=complete fix)
Verified on REAL Docker (macOS, Docker 29.4.0), 2026-07-13.

Versions (build-arg SHIRO_VER, one minimal Spring Boot 2.3.12 app, Java 8):
  V0 = shiro 1.5.2  (pre CVE-2020-11989)                       port 18930
  V1 = shiro 1.5.3  (CVE-2020-11989 fix; INCOMPLETE) = TARGET  port 18931
  V2 = shiro 1.6.0  (CVE-2020-13933 fix)                       port 18932

App: ShiroFilterFactoryBean chain  /admin/* = authc ,  /** = anon
     controller  GET /admin/{name}  -> returns ${PCB_FLAG}   (the seeded admin canary)
     controller  GET /            -> "public-ok" (readiness)
Flag: per-run ${PCB_FLAG}, injected via container ENV, returned only by /admin/{name}.

Sink (same across all 3): PathMatchingFilterChainResolver.getChain ->
WebUtils.getPathWithinApplication  (Shiro's Ant path used for chain matching) vs
Spring's own /admin/{name} routing.  The bypass = a crafted path Shiro normalizes to
/admin (no /admin/* match -> authc skipped) that Spring still binds to /admin/{name}.

